    "placesVisited": ["Anjuna Beach", "Vagator Beach", "Old Goa", "Panaji", "Dudhsagar Falls", "Spice Plantation"],
    "story": "December in Goa is everything the postcards promise and a little more. The beaches were quieter in the mornings, before the crowds arrived, and we made a habit of catching sunrise with coffee from a shack already busy with fishermen.\n\nThe Portuguese architecture of Old Goa was stunning — those white basilicas glowing in the afternoon heat. We ended each evening at a different beach shack, eating prawn curry and listening to live music. The spice plantation tour was a highlight neither of us expected: walking through rows of vanilla, cardamom, and nutmeg, learning how so much of what we cook every day starts here.\n\nIt was exactly the reset we needed."
